        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: Could not find a decreasing measure.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">The basic measures relate at each recursive call as follows:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">(&lt;, ≤, =: relation proved, ? all proofs failed, _: no proof attempted)</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">           a b c</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">1) 15:6-25 = = =</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">2) 16:6-23 = &lt; _</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">3) 17:6-23 &lt; _ _</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">Please use `termination_by` to specify a decreasing measure.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- 1)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- 2)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- 3)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"n\">decreasing_by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">all_goals</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decreasing_tactic</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It tells you that in <code>f (n+1) (m+1) (l+1)</code>, we have <code>sizeOf (n+1) = sizeOf a</code> and <code>sizeOf (m+1) = sizeOf b</code> and <code>sizeOf  (l+1) = sizeOf c</code> (by <code>rfl</code>).<br>\nIt also tells you that in <code>f (n+1) (m-1) (l)</code>, we have <code>sizeOf (n+1) = sizeOf a</code> (by <code>rfl</code>), <code>sizeOf (m-1) &lt; sizeOf b</code> (by <code>all_goals decreasing_tactic</code>) and it didn't even bother checking <code>l </code> vs <code>c</code>.<br>\nIt also tells you that in <code>f (n) (m+1) (l)</code>, we have <code>sizeOf n &lt; sizeOf a</code> (by <code>all_goals decreasing_tactic</code>) and it didn't even bother checking <code>m+1</code> vs <code>b</code> and <code>l</code> vs <code>c</code>.</p>",
